{"agent_mode": null, "bash_calls": 3, "candidate_provenance": null, "cell_seed": 3059177738203722275, "checker_exit": 0, "checker_stderr": "", "checker_stdout": "round_money rounds half up; other helpers intact\nOBENCH_VERDICT: pass\n", "checker_workspace_files": {"pricing/__init__.py": {"bytes": 0, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"}, "pricing/money.py": {"bytes": 625, "mtime": 1791872506.025948, "sha256": "e706efbc55e537831c68a4c03591bb0ba2ba058246b699a1f8e6543f687e1093"}, "tests/test_round_money.py": {"bytes": 396, "mtime": 1791872509.013783, "sha256": "48495ef045a936e6321b53ab784af9afb91f4fbae4f4af0a43b80a3ef98e952f"}, "tests/test_split.py": {"bytes": 101, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "f21bbe9cf15cf7f51ff9f71318aca4794c29f5d66cb9ae2aa0d4c919043d9bcf"}}, "child_edit_calls": 0, "child_plan_reminder": false, "cmd": ["/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/1b5c7b53d2c460b2ede60d78591b6826facf0e4d/omp", "-p", "`round_money(2.675)` returns `2.67` but customers expect `2.68`. Fix it.\n", "--mode", "json", "--provider", "vertex-anthropic", "--model", "claude-opus-5-5", "--yolo", "--session-dir", "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-38-infra-rerun/omp-38/transcripts/with/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/1/session"], "completed": true, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 2, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-38-infra-rerun/omp-38/cells/with/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/1/workspace", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/18.1.8 (/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/1b5c7b53d2c460b2ede60d78591b6826facf0e4d/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Regression test covering the reported case, the banker's-rounding trap (`round(0.125, 2) == 0.12`), and negatives:\n`round_money(2.675)` now returns `2.68`.\n\n**Cause:** there were two problems in `pricing/money.py`:\n- The float literal `2.675` is actually stored as `2.67499999\u2026`, so it really is below the halfway point.\n- Python's built-in `round()` rounds halves to the nearest even digit, not up. For example, `round(0.125, 2)` gives `0.12`. So the docstring's \"half up\" promise was wrong even for halves that are stored exactly.\n\n**Fix:** `round_money` now converts the price with `Decimal(str(x))` and rounds to cents with `ROUND_HALF_UP`. `str(x)` gives the shortest form that turns back into the same float, so the decimal is `2.675` exactly. It still returns a float, so `add_vat` (the only caller) doesn't need changes.\n\n**Test:** I added `tests/test_round_money.py`, which checks `2.675\u21922.68`, `0.125\u21920.13`, `1.005\u21921.01`, `2.674\u21922.67` and `-2.675\u2192-2.68`. Built-in `round()` gets the first two wrong (`2.67` and `0.12`). pytest isn't installed here, so I ran the new test and `test_split` directly with `python3`, and both pass. This folder isn't a git repo, so I couldn't stash the fix to watch the new test fail against the old code.\n\n**Not fixed, separate issue in `split`:** it computes `base` from `int(total * 100)`, which truncates, but computes the remainder from `round(total * 100)`. When truncation drops a cent, the remainder can equal `n` and `parts[i]` goes past the end of the list (`IndexError`). I left it alone because it's outside this fix; say if you want it fixed.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 9, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 249438, "requests_cache_write": 13100, "requests_c